        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Quadr II 5" corresp="#wit-lat"><pb n="544" ed="#liebermann"/>‘Patri<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="d" target="#QuadrII_5.lnote.oe.d"/> uenerando<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="18" target="#QuadrII_5.lnote.oe.18"/> Paschali<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#QuadrII_5.lnote.oe.12"/> summo pontifici Henricus, Dei gratia rex Anglorum, salutem! Promotioni uestre — — obedientia!’ <hi rend="italic">ed. Liebermann</hi> Quadripartitus <hi rend="italic">S</hi>. 151 <hi rend="italic">f</hi>.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text transcribed from Gesetze I p. 544 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page)</note>
